<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pheidon of Argos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">7th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pheidon was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argo">Argos</a>, probably in the 7th century BCE, who made his city the leading power of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a>. Ancient writers credited him with introducing standard weights and measures, and later tradition wrongly said he struck the first Greek coins. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> reports that he seized control of the Olympic Games, expelling the Eleans.</p></div>
